course: dictionary
lesson: 9527
title: The stingray
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stingray is a flat sea fish. Its body is wide and flat, shaped like a disc, and it has a long, thin tail. You can picture it gliding along the sand.
explain: The spine on its tail is venomous, which means it can put poison into you. But a stingray is shy, not aggressive. It uses its tail only to defend itself. «Rays are flat relatives of sharks» tells you they are related to sharks, and they hide in sand and eat shellfish and worms.
explain: Context helps here. The clues «flat» and «in the sand» tell you what a stingray looks like and where it lives, even if you have never seen one. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A stingray is a flat sea fish with a wide body shaped like a disc.
fact: «A stingray's barb on its tail is only for defence.»
fact: Stingrays are related to sharks, but their skeletons are made of cartilage, not bone.
fact: The stingray shuffle: in shallow water, slide your feet along the sand so stingrays swim away instead of being stepped on.
fact: «Hammerhead sharks sometimes pin stingrays down» with their wide heads.
exercise: «Rays are flat relatives of sharks.» What are stingrays related to? | Starfish | Whales | Snails | *Sharks
exercise: What is the stingray shuffle? | Diving deep to the bottom of the sea | *Sliding your feet in shallow water so stingrays swim away | Running fast across the sand to catch a fish | Hiding under a rock until the tide goes out
exercise: What is a stingray's tail spine for? | Swimming faster than sharks | Catching shellfish | *Defence, to protect itself | Making music
test: What shape is a stingray's body? | A cube | *A flat disc | A long tube | A ball
test: Why is a stingray not aggressive? | *It is shy and stings only to defend itself | It hunts swimmers in the sea | It likes to chase boats | It stings everyone it sees
exam: «The hammerhead's wide head sweeps the sand like a metal detector for hidden stingrays»: what does hidden mean here? | Out in the open | Very shiny | *Kept out of sight | Made of metal
